ined to 2-4, matching the four diagonal quadrants. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2934:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:41:# - Seed shapes are limited to 1x2 or 2x1. That is deliberate: with one-pixel diagonal shifts,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2935:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:48:#   diagonal marker intentionally contacts two sides. The solver now infers a diagonal from the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2936:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:51:#   for diagonal rays. The new extension translates the entire marker bbox by (±1, ±1) each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2937:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:65:#   so acceptance means all chosen diagonal markers are simultaneously legal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2938:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:68:# - A human can see several corner-attached seeds around the same '+', plus one long diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2939:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:69:#   exemplar somewhere in the grid. That makes the diagonal repetition rule and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2940:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:74:# - Generator forbids 4-neighbor contacts between foreign structures, so the diagonal strips do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2941:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:83:#   preserving only the diagonal strips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2942:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/39/code.py:87:#   horizontal side, which together encode one diagonal quadrant.\n/home/lixiny