log:2971:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:33:#      copy of the input frame ratio that can still hold the diagonal child layout with a 1-cell moat.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2972:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:48:#      Invalid now: sibling order depends only on radial distance, so layout becomes a diagonal rank display.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2973:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:53:#      diagonal items.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2974:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:277:    - Inside each frame, sort direct children by increasing centroid distance to the frame center and place them as a down-right diagonal chain with one background cell between consecutive canonical objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2975:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:627:        mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\", \"scatter\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2976:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/21/code.py:635:        elif mode == \"diagonal\":\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2977:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:19:#    as a sequence of obstacle-modules: approach diagonally on the current side,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2978:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:20:#    skim forward along the obstacle's outer side, then cross diagonally past the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2979:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:22:#    between multiple blockers before its final diagonal tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2980:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/5/code.py:329:      second-nearest (and possibly third), then keep the final diagonal heading until length runs out.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2981:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:18:#    - D1: the path is now diagonal, so each copy is shifted by (±1, ±1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2982:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:19:#    - D6: the ray no longer ends at the frame; it stops when the next diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2983:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:23:#    notch cell, so the occupied notch identifies one of four diagonals:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2984:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:33:#    the clue ray into sparse diagonal dots, while a 2x2 seed would self-overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2985:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:34:#    under unit diagonal shifts and create color-consistency ambiguity. Dominos\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2986:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:35:#    keep the diagonal repetition visually obvious and still allow both 1-color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2987:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:42:#      boundary-complete ray needed no further growth. Here a full diagonal clue\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2988:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:50:#    a diagonal domino ray and a blocker domino. Exact overlap is forbidden, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2989:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:54:#    In each sample, one ray is already expanded as a long diagonal staircase and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2990:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:57:#    both \"use the corner to choose a diagonal\" and \"stop at the blocker\" visible\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2991:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:140:    \"\"\"Return per-diagonal notch data for one plus component.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2992:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:172:    Recover the diagonal direction and the local 2-cell seed domino.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2993:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:254:def extend_repeating_tile_diagonally_until_blocked(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2994:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:263:    \"\"\"Repeat a 2-cell seed by unit diagonal translations until the next copy is blocked.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2995:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:293:    Extend corner-anchored marker dominos along diagonal rays, stopping at blockers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2996:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:301:      the corresponding diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2997:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:305:      one of the four diagonal directions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2998:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:307:      orthogonal neighbor, then copy the seed by repeated unit diagonal shifts.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:2999:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:311:    Key insight: The seed's occupied corner notch determines the diagonal, while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3000:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:346:            extend_repeating_tile_diagonally_until_blocked(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3001:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:358:# --------------- generator (output-first, diagonal + collision-stop) ---------------\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3002:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:394:    raise ValueError(\"direction must be diagonal\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3003:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:431:    \"\"\"Cells for the first `units` diagonal copies, including the seed at k=0.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3004:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:476:    \"\"\"Maximum number of full diagonal copies that fit before touching the frame.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3005:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/2/code.py:508:    \"\"\"Place one plus, one diagonal ray, and one blocker, or return None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3006:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:15:      - directions are diagonal only, so every legend is the 6x7 diagonal template\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3007:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:18:      - rooms are generated as plain rectangles so the diagonal rebound pattern is visually clean:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3008:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:40:          zigzag endpoint produced by one or more diagonal bounces\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3009:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:45:      - directions: exactly 4 diagonals\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3010:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:57:      Generator preserves that exactly with the original 6x7 diagonal legend template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3011:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:66:    - diagonal movement assumes corner-cut prevention via both orthogonal support cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3012:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:79:    - the diagonal-only restriction is visible immediately because all legends share the 6x7\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3013:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:80:      diagonal shape and no cardinal legend appears\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3014:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:95:    - because samples all show diagonal legends plus reflected endpoints, a human can infer that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3015:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:99:    - solver expects legends to decode to diagonal vectors in generated data\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3016:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:416:    Move yellow pixels inside sealed rooms according to corner legends, but only along diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3017:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:424:    - Each legend contains center and indicator marks whose offset encodes one of the four diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3018:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:429:      legend to get the initial diagonal direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3019:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:432:    - Simulate up to a fixed number of diagonal steps. When the next step hits a wall, flip the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3020:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/47/code.py:438:      \"the far wall.\" You must track a finite diagonal reflection path inside the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3021:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:25:#      each usable object is a hollow diagonal funnel whose single spike is a bbox corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3022:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:28:#      Example: suppose a NW-pointing cup has 4 interior payload pixels and the diagonal cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3023:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:31:#      D1 alone would instead paint diagonal step1..step4 continuously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3024:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:32:#      This combo erases the interior payload, walks diagonally one step at a time, paints only\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3025:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:37:#      \"advance diagonally\" decides which cell is inspected,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3026:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:41:#    - Only four diagonal directions are used; that keeps the rule legible while still requiring\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3027:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:44:#      so the sample set cannot silently degrade into plain diagonal emission or plain dashed rays.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3028:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:51:#    - Original mouth flooding used one opposite side only. For diagonal funnels that is insufficient;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3029:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:55:#      1. use a diagonal step vector,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3030:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:62:#    - The entire diagonal corridor to the edge is reserved in `occ_path`, including skipped cells,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3031:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:68:#    - From a few examples, the solver sees a corner-spike diagonal funnel, then in the output a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3032:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:78:#      and lies exactly on the continuation of the launched diagonal ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3033:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:82:#    - Assumption: the first non-bg cell on the launch diagonal is the stopping obstacle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3034:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:207:    Eject content pixels from diagonal cup-frames outward along a 45-degree tail direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3035:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:210:    - Detect the spike corner of each diagonal funnel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3036:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:213:    - Traverse diagonally outward cell by cell:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3037:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:296:    Build a diagonal funnel whose spike is the NW corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3038:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/44/code.py:377:    \"\"\"Find a placement whose diagonal corridor visibly demonstrates dash+collision.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3039:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/28/code.py:10:#    - One U endpoint has an outward-diagonal first step; that visible local direction is the D8/3 signal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3040:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/28/code.py:19:#    - The matched side is readable from shape alone: one endpoint immediately steps outward-diagonally while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3041:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88bcf3b4/28/code.py:323:    - Inspect the first step from each endpoint: the endpoint whose first move goes outward-diagonally marks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3042:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2d0172a1/19/code.py:591:    mode = random.choice((\"vertical\", \"horizontal\", \"diagonal\"))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3043:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/4/code.py:312:    \"\"\"Return a thick anti-diagonal path band that touches all four borders.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3044:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/31/code.py:31:#      drilling; diagonal disambiguation is unnecessary noise here.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3045:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:15:#    the arms of a '+'. In this combo, the seed instead sits in one diagonal corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3046:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:17:#    keep diagonal repetition clean, seeds are only 1x2 or 2x1. Each next unit is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3047:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:18:#    shifted by exactly (dr,dc) = (±1,±1), producing a zipper-like diagonal chain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3048:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:21:#    Finally, a dedicated obstacle color occupies the footprint of the next diagonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3049:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:26:#    Restricting seeds to 2 cells prevents diagonal self-overlap, keeps the mirror\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3050:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:32:#      That breaks here; seeds touch pluses only diagonally, so component lookup must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3051:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:35:#      now recovered from which diagonal corner window contains the 2-cell seed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3052:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:37:#      diagonal steps are by unit, not by rows/cols alone, and odd/even units use\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3053:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:42:#    - A pre-expanded clue component is now a long diagonal chain, not a compact seed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3054:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:46:#    The generator is output-first. For each plus it chooses a diagonal direction, a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3055:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/16/code.py:49:#    obstacle overlaps existing objects, or if a future plus would become diagonal