and the deepest diagonal color equals the seed color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3210:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:184:def _diagonal_cells(rect, corner: str, count: int, start_depth: int = 1) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3211:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:219:        for cell in _diagonal_cells(rect, corner, _max_diag_depth(rect)):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3212:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:240:        raise ValueError(\"could not infer spiral seed and diagonal palette\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3213:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:311:    Extend each wall-partitioned region into a spiral stripe pattern whose color cycle is the reverse of the diagonal depth cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3214:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:316:    - The same corner also has a short inward diagonal of distinct marker colors, ordered from shallow to deeper Chebyshev depths.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3215:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:320:    - Read the diagonal marker colors by increasing depth, reverse that list, then append the region base color to complete the repeating palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3216:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:323:    Key insight: The corner domino tells you where the spiral begins, while the diagonal tells you the palette in the opposite depth order. The outer spiral therefore starts with the deepest diagonal color, not the shallowest one.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b10624e5/_logs/13.log:3217:/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:441: